m68k backend: sincos<mode>2_68881 had no constraint on its input operand.

  internal compiler error: in print_operand_address2, at config/m68k/m68k.c:5457

with -m68881 -ffast-math (flag_unsafe_math_optimizations) on 68020/68030/68080
targets; the sincos expander is off for 68040/68060. Operand 2 of the insn was
written with an empty constraint (the expander carries "f<FP:dreg>m" on output
operand 1 instead, where it means nothing). With no constraint reload never
fixes that operand: when the pointer in its address gets no hard register, the
pointer's memory equivalence is substituted and the operand becomes the
memory-indirect address ([d,An],od), e.g. ([8,a5],1181332). This backend
rejects double-indirect addresses (decompose_one), so print_operand_address2
cannot decompose it and aborts. sin and cos of the same value in a function
with some register pressure is enough; found in a game port, 2026-10-31.

The fix gives operand 2 the constraint of the other 68881 monadic insns
(<monads><mode>2_68881). It is a crash, not wrong code: nothing that built
before changes. Checked with a rebuilt cc1: 69 C files x 3 flag sets
(-m68080 -m68881 -ffast-math, -m68020-60, -Os -m68000) give byte-identical
assembly; the failing file and a 30-line reproducer build. GCC 15.2 has no
such pattern.

--- a/gcc/config/m68k/m68k.md
+++ b/gcc/config/m68k/m68k.md
@@ -9185,9 +9185,12 @@
   "TARGET_68881 && flag_unsafe_math_optimizations && !TARGET_68060 && !TARGET_68040"
   "")
   
+;; Operand 2 needs the same constraint as the other 68881 monadic ops: with none, reload
+;; never fixes it and a spilled pointer in its address became a memory-indirect operand
+;; ([d,An],od), which print_operand_address rejects (ICE at m68k.c, -m68881 -ffast-math).
 (define_insn "sincos<mode>2_68881"
   [(set (match_operand:FP 0 "nonimmediate_operand" "=f")
-        (unspec:FP [(match_operand:FP 2 "general_operand" "")] UNSPEC_COS)
+        (unspec:FP [(match_operand:FP 2 "general_operand" "f<FP:dreg>m")] UNSPEC_COS)
    )
    (set (match_operand:FP 1 "nonimmediate_operand" "=f")
         (unspec:FP [(match_dup 2)] UNSPEC_SIN)
